# ShellCheck configuration for the praxis shell sources.
#
# Gate level is `warning`, passed on the command line by the two call sites:
# the ci.yml `shellcheck` job and scripts/run-tests.sh step 9. Both lint the
# same file set via scripts/shellcheck-files.sh — *.sh plus the extensionless
# bash-shebang CLI scripts under skills/ (issue #1175) — split into two
# invocations:
#
#   runtime (everything outside tests/) — no rule exclusions.
#   tests/                              — --exclude=SC2154,SC2034.
#
# No repo-wide disables live here any more. SC2154/SC2034 used to be disabled
# in this file, but that silenced both checks for runtime code too, while the
# rationale only ever applied to the test harness:
#
#   SC2154 — "var is referenced but not assigned": the hook tests source
#            shared fixture/helper snippets that define vars indirectly, so
#            ShellCheck can't see the assignment in the same file.
#   SC2034 — "var appears unused": test scaffolding deliberately assigns
#            capture vars (e.g. `out`) that are asserted on conditionally or
#            kept for readability.
#
# They are therefore scoped to the tests/ invocation on its command line (a
# .shellcheckrc only applies from the invocation directory — there is no
# per-subdirectory inheritance to scope them with). Runtime code keeps both
# checks; its few structural false positives (e.g. PRAXIS_FIRE_DECISION, read
# only by the EXIT trap installed in sourced hooks/_lib/record_fire.sh) carry
# targeted inline `# shellcheck disable=` directives with a reason comment.
# Genuine SC2069/SC2163/SC2164/etc. findings are fixed in the code, never
# disabled.
